{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And it shall be that the firstborn whom she bears shall stand up on the name of his dead brother.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): what is written here is the way of the Kabbalah, for the firstborn whom the dead man's wife bears shall stand up on the name of his dead brother, and this is not an actual name such that his name would be identical with his name, but rather he shall stand up on the name of his dead brother in the soul — so the verse speaks. This is what it says: ״ולא ימחה שמו מישראל״ — and his name shall not be blotted out from Israel — for if he does not stand up, his name would be blotted out from Israel, saba, and this is clear. And what the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted — ״והיה הבכור אשר תלד״, the mother of the dead man: he shall stand up in the property on the name of his dead brother, and the name of the dead man shall be mentioned in his inheritance — this is not the plain sense of the verse, but it is a midrash of the Sages, of blessed memory, and from it they proved that the obligation falls upon the eldest to perform levirate marriage, and this is why the verse used the term בכור."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:57.522590268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}